\section*{Claim}
Within the paper's fixed-parameter gluon-propagator fit, the confinement-deconfinement critical temperature is proportional to the gluon mass gap: \(T_c\approx c_{\rm conf}m_{\rm gap}\), with \(c_{\rm conf}\) dimensionless.

\section*{Premises}
\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{(P1)}\quad &x:=p^2/m_{\rm gap}^2.\\
\text{(P2)}\quad &Z_{A,{\rm fit}}(p)=\mathcal Z_A(x;\theta),\quad\text{where }\theta\text{ is a fixed dimensionless parameter set}.\\
\text{(P3)}\quad &\tau:=T/m_{\rm gap},\qquad y:=p/m_{\rm gap}.\\
\text{(P4)}\quad &p_0=2\pi T(n+\nu_j).\\
\text{(P5)}\quad &p_0^2+p^2=m_{\rm gap}^2\left[4\pi^2\tau^2(n+\nu_j)^2+y^2\right].\\
\text{(P6)}\quad &\text{In the fixed-}\theta\text{ approximation used for Eq. (49), the critical point is determined by a dimensionless degeneracy equation }\mathcal D(\tau;\theta)=0.\\
\text{(P7)}\quad &\text{The relevant solution of }\mathcal D(\tau;\theta)=0\text{ is }\tau=c_{\rm conf}.\\
\text{(P8)}\quad &m_{\rm gap}>0.
\end{aligned}
\]

\section*{Derivation}
First express the finite-temperature momentum dependence in dimensionless variables:
\begin{align}
\frac{p^2}{m_{\rm gap}^2}&=y^2 &&\text{by (P3)},\\
\frac{p_0^2+p^2}{m_{\rm gap}^2}
&=\frac{[2\pi T(n+\nu_j)]^2+p^2}{m_{\rm gap}^2} &&\text{by (P4)},\\
&=4\pi^2\left(\frac{T}{m_{\rm gap}}\right)^2(n+\nu_j)^2+\frac{p^2}{m_{\rm gap}^2},\\
&=4\pi^2\tau^2(n+\nu_j)^2+y^2 &&\text{by (P3)}.
\end{align}
Thus every appearance of the fitted gluon dressing in the finite-temperature loop depends on \(T\) and \(p\) through \(\tau\), \(y\), and the fixed parameters \(\theta\):
\begin{align}
Z_{A,{\rm fit}}\left(\sqrt{p_0^2+p^2}\right)
&=\mathcal Z_A\left(4\pi^2\tau^2(n+\nu_j)^2+y^2;\theta\right) &&\text{by (P1)--(P5)}.
\end{align}
The first-order critical point is fixed by equality of two competing minima of the dimensionless potential; by (P6), this is equivalent to
\begin{align}
\mathcal D(\tau;\theta)&=0. \label{eq:dimensionless-critical}
\end{align}
For fixed \(\theta\), (P7) gives
\begin{align}
\tau&=c_{\rm conf},\\
\frac{T_c}{m_{\rm gap}}&=c_{\rm conf} &&\text{by (P3)},\\
T_c&=c_{\rm conf}m_{\rm gap} &&\text{by (P8)}.
\end{align}
The paper denotes this proportionality as approximate because subleading dependence of \(c_{\rm conf}\) and the ghost sector may enter beyond the fixed-parameter approximation.

\section*{Final Result}
\[
\boxed{T_c\approx c_{\rm conf}m_{\rm gap}}
\]
\hfill$\blacksquare$
